    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup faces a slate defined by favorable matchups against soft pitching, highlighted by **Kyle Tucker** (77.42) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Kyle Tucker** is our primary offensive engine today; the combination of a high-ceiling base projection and the soft 5.63 xERA of Robert Gasser creates an ideal environment for him to anchor the outfield. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leverages a strong dynamic platoon advantage against G. Holmes, making him a cornerstone play at MI. We are also capitalizing on wind conditions today, which provide a tangible boost to **Sam Antonacci** (63.13) and **Miguel Vargas** (60.26), both of whom are projected to benefit significantly from favorable stadium drift against Houser.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, prioritizing efficiency against elite arms to manage our season-long game caps. **Nolan Schanuel** (44.77) was the hardest exclusion from the starting nine; while his order position remains solid, the optimizer relegated him to the pine due to the prohibitive 3.19 xERA of Nathan Eovaldi, which neutralized his upside. We are also monitoring the status of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.94); while he maintains a \"Marginal\" status, his matchup against Paul Skenes is our most dangerous of the day. Facing a sub-3.00 xERA arm significantly suppresses his output, and we are proceeding with caution. Finally, we must acknowledge that our depth is currently tested by the absence of **Gunnar Henderson**, whose game was lost to a rainout, and the ongoing IL stints for **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, forcing us to rely heavily on the remaining active roster for today\u2019s production.",
